{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeridianLinearBarOdd","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeridianLinearBarOdd","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse_near_half_u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse_near_half_u","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L93-L102","doc":"**Why the measured coefficient reads `1/2`.** The response deviates from\n`u/2` by at most `|u|³/(8π²)` — at the substrate meridian `u ≈ 0.209` this\nis `≈ 1.2×10⁻⁴`, far below the linear term, so the ladder fit returns\n`a = 1/2` to the observed precision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.half_u_sub_response","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.half_u_sub_response","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**Exact `u/2` deficit identity.** The response equals `u/2` minus an\nexplicit cubic remainder: `u/2 − resp(u) = u³ / (2(u² + 4π²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.volChannel_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.volChannel_even","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The bar-even volume channel, for contrast.** For an even volume function\n(4₁ is amphichiral: `Vol(−u) = Vol(u)`), the volume term of the growth\nrate is even in `u` — the bar-EVEN channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse_odd","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L67-L74","doc":"**Bar-odd parity.** The bar involution `σ : q ↦ q⁻¹` acts on the meridian\nas `u ↦ −u`; the linear-meridian response is an odd function of `u` —\na bar-ODD channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.alpha_resid_of_meridian_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.alpha_resid_of_meridian_term","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L55-L65","doc":"**The response of an `Im S(u) ⊃ π·u` term is exactly\n`meridianLinearResponse`.** Adding `π·u` to the volume in the growth-rate\nformula `2π·(…)/(u² + 4π²)` shifts it by exactly the response model —\nthe algebraic content of \"the measured residual is the `π·u` term\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.meridianLinearResponse","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianLinearBarOdd.lean#L49-L53","doc":"Growth-rate residual produced by a linear meridian term `π·u` in `Im S(u)`:\n`2π²·u / (u² + 4π²)` — the model measured in PR #3691 with the leading\ncoefficient `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}